        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fa0d88522a894ddc87b6db41a219e800",
      "statement": "A fresh begin ensures code-mode repository setup (creating the scheduled workflow only on init), builds a source fingerprint, and persists .run.json state plus interrupted last-update metadata; an init begin additionally opens a recoverable wiki replacement that is committed only after run state and interrupted metadata are durable, and rolled back if begin itself fails.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/generation/repository-run.ts#L252-L289",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:91ab1905969c4f140755a1fa50662671db9f26468c93d2df5cf870b1c2db4c15:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/generation/repository-run.ts#L371-L416",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d1f17a9143d645d0a20adbf60391dc424fb7a40fb27ebbe5d6638e894896498d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_38dc326b6b264296bcc682601bb1e8f4",
      "statement": "A later begin that finds a persisted .run.json reconstructs the interrupted run, validating that mode, language, and producer actor match; if the recomputed source fingerprint has drifted it invalidates the whole persisted plan and resets the phase to planning so the host must submit a fresh plan, otherwise the existing plan is preserved and generation continues.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/generation/repository-run.ts#L426-L510",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d17b4fdf44efa3fbf9fc36f590ddd423e585f913e4c7911ebe7740b0ddb1465b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d3bfd2fdc0ff4530bc9400753e881d61",
      "statement": "openwiki_finish finalizes artifacts, Claims, and metadata only after every PageJob is complete: it re-checks the source fingerprint, applies abandoned and planned deletions, reconciles deleted Claims sidecars, runs deterministic finalizers, finalizes Claims with a whole-run durability proof, re-checks the fingerprint across the finish window, persists complete metadata only when content changed, and removes .run.json last so any earlier failure leaves the run resumable for retry.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/generation/repository-run.ts#L993-L1055",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:16af8feab1e08b2f76d90b8f1a7f927d74119462d91248f7055eb94bd94f2568:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0ce05bdab6a041828743fa93189f7736",
      "statement": "HostSessionManager serializes lifecycle operations through a single in-progress flag (rejecting a concurrent operation with invalid_state) and holds at most one active run at a time; operations other than begin select the active run via requireSession, which throws invalid_state when no run is active or the supplied runId does not match the active run's durable ID.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/integrations/core/session-manager.ts#L260-L298",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bdf83eb51b5cf5cd8ea5c0436660fdfb5e479608224886ba1f0b6f751006e24d:"
        },
        {
